    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30508" root="عمد" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَمَّدٌ</span></b> , applied to a tent, <i>Set up with poles:</i>
(O, K:) occurring in a verse of [the Mo'allakah
of] Tarafeh [p. 88 in the EM]. (O. [See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْمَدٌ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشْىٌ مُعَمَّدٌ</span> (O, K, TA, in some copies
of the K <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَىْءٌ</span>,) <i>A sort of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشْى</span> [or <i>variegated
cloth</i>] (O, K, TA) [<i>figured</i>] <i>with the form of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِمَاد</span>
[app. meaning <i>lofty buildings</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمُدَّانٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمُدٌّ</span>: and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمِيدٌ</span>.

